GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC14): BlobShadowDark draws the blobs under people, the follower
and NPCs (GameShadow 1) faint: their polygon alpha lowered until they darken by at most that much
(as SoftenGameShadows does for the painted ones). The user (2026-11-18): the blobs stand for the
moon's light by night, and at the game's strength (about 24%) they looked too dark.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

--- a/src/GPU3D_Soft.h	2026-11-18 19:55:29.356141033 -0500
+++ b/src/GPU3D_Soft.h	2026-11-18 19:55:38.043600706 -0500
@@ -116,6 +116,10 @@
     // are.
     bool SoftenGameShadows = false;
     static constexpr float SoftShadowDark = 0.03f;
+    // GoldLink (patch 0033): the blobs under people (GameShadow 1) drawn faint, darkening at most
+    // this much (0: as the game draws them): by night they stand for the moon's light, and at the
+    // game's strength (about 0.24) they looked too dark (the user, 2026-11-18).
+    float BlobShadowDark = 0.0f;
 
     void SetupRenderThread(GPU& gpu);
     void EnableRenderThread();
@@ -126,8 +130,8 @@
     // without its wrapping bits, and the palette).
     ShadowGeometry ShownGeometry, RenderedGeometry;
